## What
The in-session human approval surface #827 asked for, deferred to 1.4 (owner decision 2026-09-26). 1.3.1 ships the honest fail-closed subset: with no surface attached, `AutonomyController.request_autonomy` returns status `"unavailable"` (never a silent `"pending"`), `AutonomyLevelTool` reports that no human approver is attached, and `ModeSwitchTool` fails when there is no runtime to apply a mode to.

## Build
One real approval surface (interactive display + console) that attaches through `AutonomyController.set_approval_surface`:
- shows the model's stated reason **and the recent tool results**, so an approver can see what triggered the request;
- resolves requests through `approve_autonomy_request` / `reject_autonomy_request`, and later mode requests;
- never auto-approves in non-interactive runs for escalations the policy says need a human — the generic confirmation path auto-answers "yes" and must not be reused;
- a time-boxed `singularity` grant that survives the re-exec a mode switch performs (`cli_utils.py::reexec_with_mode`) — the #821 design's original intent.

Related: #821, #827, #828.
